    "description": "D15: a staff-engineer reviewer on Sol 6.2 (eval only)\n\nD15: a skeptical staff-engineer reviewer on Sol 6.2, as an experiment in the eval only. It adds no reviewer to the shipped pipeline. The note is `docs/research/d15-staff-reviewer.md`.\n\n## Result\n\nBeside the six specialists, the staff reviewer (Sol 6.2 at medium effort, through the Codex CLI) raises recall from 0.448 / 0.544 to 0.544 / 0.608 and precision from 0.412 / 0.430 to 0.469 / 0.478. The two figures are the two baseline repeats of the specialists, on the same first verifier (Sonnet 5.5 medium, replay). It finds 8 known items that no specialist found in either repeat, and 7 of them are blocking. It is the slowest reviewer in 27 of 28 cases (57 s against 31 s at the median). Only 1 of its 4 refactor recommendations posts, as a nit, because the verifier rejects old-code items. No finding names a principle without a cost.\n\nQuota: about 1.5 to 1.75 points of the Codex 5-hour window and 0.2 of the week for each review, so about 55 to 65 reviews per window and about 480 per week. Plan: $18.04 for the verifier step and its judge calls.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `prompts/staff-reviewer.md`: the reviewer prompt, from the user's draft. Each claim starts with a tag that maps to a category of the finding schema.\n- `pr-review eval-codex-review --prompt <file>`: run a named prompt under `prompts/` in place of `general-review`; `--effort` accepts `max`. With no `--prompt`, the command does what it did before.\n- `docs/research/d15-staff-reviewer.md`: the note, with every figure, by size and for walle and websites apart, the 10 examples, the refactor items with the verifier's view, the cost, the quota and the time, the limits, and what the user decides.\n- `TICKETS.md`: D15, done.\n- The version goes to 0.21.0.\n\n## Open for the user\n\nWhether to add the reviewer, and how it would run in CI: the Codex CLI needs a login there, and rule 4 of CLAUDE.md keeps credentials out of the code.\n\n## Checks\n\n`npm test` (1713 passed), `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck` and `npm run build` pass.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01XrBTZdfE1rqbczPpmGQQ5S\n",
